From 210ac22d446c8e2625b091e79256806b836eee20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Daer <jeremy@37signals.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:42:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid dynamic regexp in safe_constantize LoadError handling

`safe_constantize` built a `Regexp` from the constant name, unescaped,
to check a `LoadError` message, so a caller passing untrusted input,
such as an Action Cable subscribe command, chose the pattern the
server compiled.

Match the name's first segment as a literal string instead, and add a
CHANGELOG entry.

[CVE-2026-126080]
[GHSA-8474-xrp6-wh69]

[ Upstream commit 210ac22d446c8e2625b091e79256806b836eee20 ]
https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/210ac22d446c8e2625b091e79256806b836eee20

[Shivani: Modified to apply on activesupport-7.1.3.4. Removed test and CHANGELOG changes]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
 lib/active_support/inflector/methods.rb | 20 ++------------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/active_support/inflector/methods.rb b/lib/active_support/inflector/methods.rb
--- a/lib/active_support/inflector/methods.rb
+++ b/lib/active_support/inflector/methods.rb
@@ -319,7 +319,8 @@
         e.name.to_s == camel_cased_word.to_s)
     rescue LoadError => e
       message = e.respond_to?(:original_message) ? e.original_message : e.message
-      raise unless /Unable to autoload constant #{const_regexp(camel_cased_word)}/.match?(message)
+      constant_name = camel_cased_word.split("::").find { |part| !part.empty? } || camel_cased_word
+      raise unless message.include?("Unable to autoload constant #{constant_name}")
     end
 
     # Returns the suffix that should be added to a number to denote the position
@@ -349,23 +350,6 @@
     end
 
     private
-      # Mounts a regular expression, returned as a string to ease interpolation,
-      # that will match part by part the given constant.
-      #
-      #   const_regexp("Foo::Bar::Baz") # => "Foo(::Bar(::Baz)?)?"
-      #   const_regexp("::")            # => "::"
-      def const_regexp(camel_cased_word)
-        parts = camel_cased_word.split("::")
-
-        return Regexp.escape(camel_cased_word) if parts.empty?
-
-        last = parts.pop
-
-        parts.reverse!.inject(last) do |acc, part|
-          part.empty? ? acc : "#{part}(::#{acc})?"
-        end
-      end
-
       # Applies inflection rules for +singularize+ and +pluralize+.
       #
       # If passed an optional +locale+ parameter, the uncountables will be
